@startuml seq-commits-log
'' ============================================================================
'' vinary-viewer — Sequence: the Commits sidebar tab's log delivery (ADR-0039).
''
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because one set of lifelines has to carry a mount
'' phase, two parallel async requests, a generation-guarded reply, a stored
'' incremental fold, and a debounced watcher push — `== phase ==` dividers and
'' `alt` keep every leg on the same seam-colored lanes.
'' ============================================================================
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title Commits tab — mount, paged log, stored lane fold, live refresh

autonumber "0:"

actor User #white
participant "ui.commits\ncommits-panel" as Panel RENDERER_TINT
participant "re-frame\nevents / fx" as RF REFRAME_TINT
participant "app-db\n[:ui :commits :repos <root>]" as Db APPDB_TINT
participant "preload `window.vv`" as Vv IPC_TINT
participant "main.git\n(async run-git)" as Git MAIN_TINT
participant "git CLI" as CLI FS_TINT
participant "Chokidar\n(.git watcher)" as Watch FS_TINT

== panel mount (root = pin > deepest containing project > last shown > first) ==
User -> Panel : open the **Commits** sidebar tab
Panel -> RF : `[:commits/shown root]`\n(component-did-mount; panel keyed by root)
RF -> Db : `:last-root` ← root
RF -> Vv : `gitWatch([root])`\n**vv:git-watch**
Vv -> Git : `sync-owner-roots!`\n(tree-watcher-twin ownership)
Git -> CLI : `rev-parse --absolute-git-dir`\n+ `--git-common-dir`\n(worktree-safe: HEAD and refs\ncan live in different dirs)
CLI --> Git : the two directories
Git -> Watch : watch [git-dir/**HEAD**,\ncommon-dir/**packed-refs**,\ncommon-dir/**refs**]\n{ignoreInitial, depth 4}
RF -> RF : `[:commits/ensure root]`\n(idempotent: branches if missing,\npage 0 if empty)

== branches (the combo's data) ==
RF -> Vv : `gitBranches {root}`\n**vv:git-branches**
Vv -> Git : `handle-branches`
Git -> CLI : `for-each-ref\n--format=%(refname)%1f\n%(refname:short)%1f%(HEAD)`\n+ `rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`
CLI --> Git : ref rows + head name\n(detached → short hash)
Git --> Vv : {head, detached?, branches\n[{name, kind, current?}]}
Vv --> RF : `[:commits/branches-received]`
RF -> Db : `:branches` ← payload\n(a vanished viewed ref → nil,\nfall back to HEAD)

== page 0 (and every "Load more") ==
RF -> Db : `:loading?` ← true; **:gen++**\n(stale-reply guard)
RF -> Vv : `gitLog {root, skip, limit 250, ref?}`\n**vv:git-log**
Vv -> Git : `handle-log`
Git -> CLI : `rev-parse --verify --quiet\n--end-of-options <ref>^{commit}`\n(only when a ref was given)
Git -> CLI : `git log **--date-order**\n--max-count=250 --skip=N\n--pretty=<9-field %x1f/%x00>\n--end-of-options <ref>`
CLI --> Git : NUL-terminated records\n(children strictly before parents —\nthe lane precondition)
Git -> Git : `glog/parse-log`\n(9 fields + 40-hex validated;\nhostile records dropped)
Git --> Vv : {commits, exhausted, empty?}\n— structured, never raw text
Vv --> RF : `[:commits/log-received\nroot gen page0?]`

alt gen is current
  RF -> Db : append `:commits`;\n**stored incremental fold** (R2):\n`graph/assign` state ⟶\n`:graph {:rows :state :max-lane}`\n(one fold site — rail now,\nCommit Graph document later)
  Db -> Panel : `:commits/for-root` fires
  Panel -> Panel : per row: self-contained SVG **rail cell**\n(prev row's edge targets = top-half ink,\nown edges = dot + through ink);\nGFM body only on expand
  Panel --> User : list + lane rail\n(+ "Load more (N shown)")
else superseded request
  RF -> RF : reply dropped
end

== live refresh (vv:git-changed) ==
User -> CLI : commit / fetch / tag /\nbranch switch — any terminal
CLI -> Watch : HEAD / refs / packed-refs change
Watch -> Git : fs events
Git -> Git : **debounce 300 ms per root**\n(a fetch touches many refs —\nthe panel needs ONE refresh)
Git -> Vv : push **vv:git-changed** {root}\n(to owning windows only)
Vv -> RF : `[:commits/git-changed]`
RF -> RF : loaded repos only:\nbranches + **page-0 replace**\n(:gen++ strands in-flight replies)
RF -> Db : page 0 refolds from `init-state`;\n`keep-surviving` prunes selection /\nexpanded / bodies **by hash**
Db -> Panel : re-render ≤ ~1 s after the change,\nselection intact
Panel --> User : fresh history, place kept

== unmount ==
Panel -> RF : `[:commits/hidden]`\n(sidebar collapsed / tab switched)
RF -> Vv : `gitWatch([])`\n**vv:git-watch**
Vv -> Git : release this window's ownership
Git -> Watch : close the repo's watcher\nwhen the last owner leaves

note over Git, CLI
  Strictly READ-ONLY: `log`, `for-each-ref`, `rev-parse` —
  argv arrays, no shell; every user-supplied ref sits behind
  `--end-of-options` AND rev-parse pre-validation.
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| Renderer / UI (ui.commits) |
  |<#4F97D7>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| re-frame events / fx |
  |<#7590DB>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| app-db ([:ui :commits]) |
  |<#B1951D>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| IPC seam |
  |<#3A5BA0>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| MAIN (vinary.main.git) |
  |<#9F8766>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| git CLI / Chokidar |
endlegend
@enduml
